# L §5.11: "Every exact value is capped at 4 096 decimal digits in its numerator and its denominator; above that
# it is refused at that key (RUN-DIGITS)".  pow(10, 5000) has 5 001 digits; pow(10, 4000) has 4 001.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"

input x: num
input big: int
input ok: int

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  x = 10
  big = 5000
  ok = 4000

ask q1: pow(x, big)
ask q2: pow(x, ok) > x
=== expect
q1: refused: RUN-DIGITS ...
  cut 2026-12-31
q2: true
  cut 2026-12-31
